-- title:
--   Triviality of all Cartier pairings forces a completed point to vanish
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, let $K$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p/\mathbb{Q}_p$ that is finite over $\mathbb{Q}_p$, and let $R$ be a commutative ring with an algebra structure over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p$ such that the image of $R$ is exactly $\{x : x \in K,\ \|x\| \le 1\}$ (hypothesis `hR`) and the structure map is injective (`hinj`). Let $G, G'$ be $p$-divisible groups over $R$ of height $h$, i.e. systems of finite free cocommutative Hopf $R$-algebras `level v` of rank $p^{vh}$ with surjective coalgebra-algebra transition maps whose kernels are the ideals generated by the image of the augmentation ideal under multiplication by $p^v$, and let $D$ be a Cartier duality datum between them: isomorphisms $G'.\mathrm{level}\,v \simeq \mathrm{Hom}_R(G.\mathrm{level}\,v, R)$ compatible with the transition maps and multiplication by $p$, giving pairings `D.pair` on level-$w$ points with values in the coefficient algebra. Write $\mathcal{O}$ for the integral closure of $R$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p$. Let $g$ be a completed point of $G$ over $R$, that is a family of points $g_i \in G(R/p^iR)$ compatible under reduction. Assume: for every element $y$ of the Tate module of $G'(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p)$, that is a sequence $(y_n)$ with $p^n y_n = 0$ and $p\,y_{n+1} = y_n$, all $i \le w$, every level-$w$ point $f$ of $G$ over $\mathcal{O}/p^i\mathcal{O}$ whose image in $G(\mathcal{O}/p^i\mathcal{O})$ is the $i$-th component of the image of $g$ under the base change $R \to \mathcal{O}$, and every level-$w$ point $\psi$ of $G'$ over $\mathcal{O}$ whose image in $G'(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p)$ is $y_w$, the pairing of $f$ with the reduction of $\psi$ modulo $p^i$ equals $1$. Then $g = 0$.
--
--   This is Step 4 of the proof of Tate's Proposition 11 on $p$-divisible groups over a complete discrete valuation ring of mixed characteristic, here with base the ring of integers of a finite extension $K/\mathbb{Q}_p$ presented abstractly through its embedding into $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p$; equivalently, it is the injectivity half of the map $G(R) \to \mathrm{Hom}(T(G'), U)$ of Tate's Theorem 3. It is used in establishing linear independence statements for the Tate module of the dual over the $p$-adic complex numbers.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_PDivisibleGroup_CartierDuality_cpoints_eq_zero_of_forall_pair_eq_one_of_forall_mem_range_iff.lean

